  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a reader, I want the app to remember where I stopped in each topic, so that I resume there on any screen, window or launch.\n\n### Scope\n\nPer-account, per-topic store: last page, last read message number (`numreponse`), last visit date. Positions only move forward unless the caller says otherwise; bounded size with eviction of the oldest topics. Protocol + file + in-memory implementations (Linux tests).\n\n- Module: HFRStorage · Difficulty: easy · Priority: medium · post-MVP\n- Implements: FEAT-001 (#145), FEAT-007 (#151), FEAT-015 (#159)\n- Absorbs: FEATURES.md 'new reading-position store'; ultra-hfr decisions D8–D9 (bybifok-proposals §3)\n- Legacy sources (read-only, `origin/master`): none in legacy (new capability); last-read anchors of `MessagesView.swift` (HFR-002, HFR-009 in legacy backlog.md)\n- Spec: `docs/lots/LOT-090-*.md`\n\n### Depends on\n\n- LOT-013 (#46, done)\n\n### Feature umbrella\n\n- Implements FEAT-001 (#145), proposed by Bybifok (credit in the spec, PR and CREDITS.md). Other lots of this feature: LOT-092 (#184), LOT-143 (#233), LOT-144 (#234); the last lot (LOT-144 (#234)) closes #145.\n- Implements FEAT-007 (#151), proposed by Bybifok (credit in the spec, PR and CREDITS.md). Other lots of this feature: LOT-111 (#202); the last lot (LOT-111 (#202)) closes #151.\n- Implements FEAT-015 (#159), proposed by Bybifok (credit in the spec, PR and CREDITS.md). Other lots of this feature: LOT-145 (#235); the last lot (LOT-145 (#235)) closes #159.\n\nFEAT issues (#145–#165) are umbrellas and are never claimed: claim this lot's issue; the PR says `Closes #<this issue>` and `Refs #<FEAT issue>`.\n\n### Model\n\nSonnet → Opus (AGENTS.md §6: the reviewer is never the author model)\n\n### Captures needed\n\n- none known; any page state the spec needs and the fixtures lack is listed as *pending capture*, never hand-built (LESSONS 35-36)\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `ReadingPositionStore` keyed by account and `TopicID`; `advance(to:)` never moves backwards, `reset` is explicit.\n- [ ] Bounded (configurable count) with oldest-first eviction; corrupted file → empty store reported as a typed error, never a crash.\n- [ ] Account removal API drops that account's positions.\n- [ ] Swift Testing tests; `swift test` green on Linux and macOS CI; module rules of docs/ARCHITECTURE.md respected (`scripts/check-lot-deps.py` passes).\n- [ ] Spec `docs/lots/LOT-090-*.md` with legacy sources (file:line), edge cases and intentional differences; verified protocol facts in HFR-PROTOCOL §6c under this lot's own `###`.\n\n### Before you start (agents and humans)\n\nRead, in order: AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, docs/agents/ORCHESTRATION.md, docs/agents/REVIEW-ROUNDS.md, docs/agents/LESSONS.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, App/README.md, ADR 0012, the spec of every dependency (docs/lots/), docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md for any forum fact, docs/FIXTURES.md if captures are involved. Claim with `/claim <session-id>` on this issue before writing code; PR body `Closes #<this issue>` + `Claim: <session-id>`; never guess HFR behaviour (stop and list the captures needed).",
